cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this research prototype, its method, or its measured results,
  please cite it using these metadata.
title: Graph-Aware Fault Detection for an OpenTitan HMAC Circuit
abstract: >-
  A supervised hybrid classifier for predicting single stuck-at fault
  detectability in a synthesized OpenTitan HMAC/SHA-256 circuit. The model fuses
  a leakage-safe per-sample feature branch with a directed simplified graph
  convolution branch computed over the gate-level netlist, giving 646 input
  features and 93,185 trainable parameters. Evaluated on 438,528 held-out
  samples it reaches balanced accuracy 0.8166, ROC-AUC 0.9166 and Brier score
  0.1210 at a locked decision threshold of 0.4965. The model uses
  no post-simulation features and no labels during graph propagation, so
  structural and behavioural evidence remain disjoint. Developed under a staged
  protocol with pre-registered acceptance criteria, pinned synthesis and
  simulation toolchains, and hash-anchored freeze artifacts for every stage.
